I would add two more more complex tests which is:

```C#
public interface IA { }
public interface IB { }
public interface IC { }
public class A : IA { }
public class B : IA { B(IA a) { } }
public class C : IA { C(IB b) { } }
```

```C#
IServiceCollection descriptors = new ServiceCollection();
descriptors.AddTransient<IA, A>();
descriptors.AddTransient<IB, B>();
descriptors.AddTransient(typeof(IC), typeof(C));
var provider = descriptors.BuildServiceProvider();
provider.GetService<IC>().Method();
```

and an open generic registration:

```C#
public class Logger<T> { }
public interface IA { }
public class A : IA { }
```

```C#
IServiceCollection descriptors = new ServiceCollection();
descriptors.AddTransient<IA, A>();
descriptors.AddTransient(typeof(ILogger<>), typeof(Logger<>));
var provider = descriptors.BuildServiceProvider();
provider.GetService<ILogger<IA>>().Method();
```

and an IEnumerable<T> resolution:

```C#
public interface IA { }
public class A1 : IA { }
public class A2 : IA { }
```

```C#
IServiceCollection descriptors = new ServiceCollection();
descriptors.AddTransient<IA, A1>();
descriptors.AddTransient<IA, A2>();
provider.GetServices<IA>().Method(); // Under the covers calls `GetService<IEnumerable<T>>`
```
